{"title":"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1_(desperation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1 (desperation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are randomly chosen without replacement from the set of integers with absolute value not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the probability that the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/1/a5167f86a8ed400b306f0193631cfcc02ccd4981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 + ax^2 + bx + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distinct integer roots?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/9/d49c39f1bddbdcf7b3dbfc5d27fb21b958220da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{240} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{1}{221} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{105} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{1}{84} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{1}{63}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"448\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f63eea55eee86a2cf0db5afd5a8ef31d9a5c6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10 \\le a,b \\le 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />, there are 21 integers to choose from, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfc31b2c97aec57be821a1d584b312c3aefadeca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(21,2) = 21 \\times 20 = 420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"200\" height=\"20\" /> equally likely ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Applying Vieta's formulas, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10ef58f9174ea676d4258e173f258da983cb67ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 \\cdot x_2  \\cdot x_3  = -6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/1/7010ba21aa24f9fe0e9e76562b31e8fc7d094f60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 + x_2+ x_3 = -a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a473197df3e30dd337b161c8534387addde8e59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 \\cdot x_2 + x_1 \\cdot x_3  + x_3 \\cdot x_2  = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"225\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Cases:\n</p><p>(1)  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/72623bf0b5bf0bdce056aa258a1e1df8d5437a23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,x_2,x_3)  = (-1,1,6) , b = -1, a=-6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"310\" height=\"20\" />  valid \n</p><p>(2)  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a42db4fea97944e17aa595123b553a99b6a70a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,x_2,x_3)  = ( 1,2,-3) , b = -7, a=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"296\" height=\"20\" />  valid \n</p><p>(3)  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c99a6b53895bb77954c74a615b10d872de21175f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,x_2,x_3)  = (1,-2,3) , b = -5, a=-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"310\" height=\"20\" />  valid \n</p><p>(4)  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/6/2763b980b171a407e722019a8752b76ff1b20248.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,x_2,x_3)  = (-1,2,3) , b = 1, a=-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"296\" height=\"20\" />  valid \n</p><p>(5)  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29ff96e4fe25aa12eeb6ed8cf2e4b778865e26ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,x_2,x_3)  = (-1,-2,-3) , b = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"268\" height=\"20\" /> invalid \n</p><p>the total event space is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f465cd47ea9e0e0fee045713cd0913d495bcd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21  \\cdot (21- 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" /> (choice of select a times choice of selecting b given no-replacement) \n</p><p>hence, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/2/112d9ca1729e23734581d965c05f020561479ac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{21 \\cdot 20} =   \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{1}{105}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"157\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1.1_.28desperation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1_(desperation)\">Solution 1.1 (desperation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1 (desperation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As obtained in Solution 1, we get that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/35785ea2ab94ca8e30c9ebd83a03576aa084f014.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(21,2) = 420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" /> equally likely ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, which means that the denominator will likely be a factor of 420, which leaves answers C and D, and if you are lucky enough, you can guess that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4da5136109b372e21e8d857c8805a251e09131.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{1}{105}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"79\" height=\"49\" />. If you're not lucky enough, however, that's a math instinct skill issue, and I recommend you get instinct first before you do math. \n</p><p>~Soupboy0, ShortPeopleFartalot\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ptFW2866-Xw\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ptFW2866-Xw</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B\">2024 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" a